    "closed": true,
    "closedAt": "2025-04-30T10:49:35Z",
    "comment_count": 1,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author": {
                "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24854248?u=d09fd974c6720eba3039db6beb2f1c1efecdb51d&v=4",
                "login": "echasnovski",
                "resourcePath": "/echasnovski",
                "url": "https://github.com/echasnovski"
            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Yes:\r\n- See the applied background+foreground colors as `guibg` + `guifg` fields of `:hi Normal`.\r\n- Create a '~/.config/nvim/colors/my_beautiful_scheme.lua' file.\r\n- Populate it with contents similar to ['randomhue' color scheme file](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/colors/randomhue.lua):\r\n    ```lua\r\n    require('mini.hues').setup({\r\n      -- Replace 'background' and 'foreground' with colors you prefer\r\n      background = '#112233',\r\n      foreground = '#ddeeff',\r\n      n_hues = 8,\r\n      saturation = vim.o.background == 'dark' and 'medium' or 'high',\r\n      accent = 'bg',\r\n    })\r\n\r\n    vim.g.colors_name = 'my_beautiful_scheme'\r\n    ```\r\n\r\nThis can now be used as `:colorscheme my_beautiful_scheme`.",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Yes:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>See the applied background+foreground colors as <code class=\"notranslate\">guibg</code> + <code class=\"notranslate\">guifg</code> fields of <code class=\"notranslate\">:hi Normal</code>.</li>\n<li>Create a '~/.config/nvim/colors/my_beautiful_scheme.lua' file.</li>\n<li>Populate it with contents similar to <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/colors/randomhue.lua\">'randomhue' color scheme file</a>:\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"require('mini.hues').setup({\n  -- Replace 'background' and 'foreground' with colors you prefer\n  background = '#112233',\n  foreground = '#ddeeff',\n  n_hues = 8,\n  saturation = vim.o.background == 'dark' and 'medium' or 'high',\n  accent = 'bg',\n})\n\nvim.g.colors_name = 'my_beautiful_scheme'\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-c1\">require</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>mini.hues<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>).<span class=\"pl-c1\">setup</span>({\n  <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">--</span> Replace 'background' and 'foreground' with colors you prefer</span>\n  <span class=\"pl-smi\">background</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>#112233<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>,\n  <span class=\"pl-smi\">foreground</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>#ddeeff<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>,\n  <span class=\"pl-smi\">n_hues</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">8</span>,\n  <span class=\"pl-smi\">saturation</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">o</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">background</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">==</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>dark<span class=\"pl-pds\">' </span></span><span class=\"pl-k\">and</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>medium<span class=\"pl-pds\">' </span></span><span class=\"pl-k\">or</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>high<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>,\n  <span class=\"pl-smi\">accent</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>bg<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>,\n})\n\n<span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">g</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">colors_name</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>my_beautiful_scheme<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span></pre></div>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This can now be used as <code class=\"notranslate\">:colorscheme my_beautiful_scheme</code>.</p>",
            "bodyText": "Yes:\n\nSee the applied background+foreground colors as guibg + guifg fields of :hi Normal.\nCreate a '~/.config/nvim/colors/my_beautiful_scheme.lua' file.\nPopulate it with contents similar to 'randomhue' color scheme file:\nrequire('mini.hues').setup({\n  -- Replace 'background' and 'foreground' with colors you prefer\n  background = '#112233',\n  foreground = '#ddeeff',\n  n_hues = 8,\n  saturation = vim.o.background == 'dark' and 'medium' or 'high',\n  accent = 'bg',\n})\n\nvim.g.colors_name = 'my_beautiful_scheme'\n\n\nThis can now be used as :colorscheme my_beautiful_scheme.",
